# A unified diff encodes a blank CONTEXT line as a single space, so trailing whitespace in a .patch
# file is load-bearing: strip it and the patch stops applying. `git diff --check` (the diff-check
# gate) flags those as errors, which made adding or editing ANY carried patch fail CI.
#
# It was latent rather than new: after-ordering.patch and cli-null-next-run.patch already carry
# blank context lines and were simply never part of a diff after the gate was introduced.
patches/**/*.patch -whitespace
